r","email":"wernedc@auburn.edu"},{"first_name":"David","last_name":"Werneke","role":"Collections Manager","email":"wernedc@auburn.edu"},{"first_name":"Laura","last_name":"Russell","role":"Programmer","email":"larussell@vertnet.org"},{"first_name":"David","last_name":"Bloom","role":"Coordinator","email":"dbloom@vertnet.org"},{"first_name":"John","last_name":"Wieczorek","role":"Information Architect","email":"tuco@berkeley.edu"},{"first_name":"Jonathon","last_name":"Armbruster","role":"Curator of Fishes","email":"armbrjw@mail.auburn.edu"},{"first_name":"David","last_name":"Werneke","role":"Collections Manager","email":"wernedc@auburn.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC0","publisher":"842a2bb5-d705-4d6c-8401-abf3ca28c05d","totalCount":87245,"hitRatio":0.00008023382428792481},{"uuid":"ce0c9488-97f0-432a-a0fa-d204230366be","itemCount":3,"name":"UAIC Ichthyological Collection","description":"The State of Alabama contains the most diverse fish fauna of North America.  The University of Alabama Ichthyological Collection (UAIC) documents this diversity and is one of the largest educational and research collections of fishes in the southeastern United States.  This nationally and internationally recognized biological resource includes over one million preserved, skeletal, and frozen specimens, some dating back to the mid 1900's, and is the best single resource documenting past and present distributions and abundances of fishes in the State.","logo":"http://ipt.vertnet.org:8080/ipt/logo.do?r=uaic_fish","url":"http://uaic.as.ua.edu","emllink":"https://ipt.vertnet.org/eml.do?r=uaic_fish","archivelink":"https://ipt.vertnet.org/archive.do?r=uaic_fish","contacts":[{"first_name":"Worth","last_name":"Pugh","role":"Coordinator of Zoological Collections","email":"mwpugh@ua.edu"},{"first_name":"Worth","last_name":"Pugh","role":"Coordinator of Zoological Collections","email":"mwpugh@ua.edu"},{"first_name":"Laura","last_name":"Russell","role":"Programmer","email":"larussell@vertnet.org"},{"first_name":"David","last_name":"Bloom","role":"Coordinator","email":"dbloom@vertnet.org"},{"first_name":"John","last_name":"Wieczorek","role":"Information Architect","email":"tuco@berkeley.edu"},{"first_name":"Phillip","last_name":"Harris","role":"Associate Professor and Curator of Fishes","email":"pharris@bama.ua.edu"},{"first_name":"Worth","last_name":"Pugh","role":"Coordinator of Zoological Collections","email":"mwpugh@ua.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC0","publisher":"842a2bb5-d705-4d6c-8401-abf3ca28c05d","totalCount":126702,"hitRatio":0.00002367760572050954},{"uuid":"c38b867b-05f3-4733-802e-d8d2d3324f84","itemCount":2,"name":"UF FLMNH Ichthyology","description":"The UF Fish Collection, dating to 1917, contains 214,205 lots and 2,300,803 specimens. Included are representatives of 8,250 species from 400 families. The collection includes 93 primary types and approximately 1,600 lots of secondary types representing 563 species. Also in the collection are 5,825 specimens of disarticulated and articulated skeletons representing 875 species. Especially notable are historic collections of large and important marine fishes as well as rapidly growing collections of freshwater fishes from Southeast Asia. In 2006, the museum expanded its program to archive frozen tissue samples with a newly established UF Genetic Resources Collection. Tissues of fishes are stored in -20ºC freezers and number 4,150 samples of 900 species. All specimens and tissues are databased online and available for loan.","url":"","emllink":"https://ipt.floridamuseum.ufl.edu/ipt/eml.do?r=ichthyology","archivelink":"https://ipt.floridamuseum.ufl.edu/ipt/archive.do?r=ichthyology","contacts":[{"first_name":"Rob","last_name":"Robins","role":"Ichthyology Collection Manager","email":"rhrobins@flmnh.ufl.edu"},{"first_name":"Rob","last_name":"Robins","role":"Ichthyology Collection Manager","email":"rhrobins@flmnh.ufl.edu"},{"first_name":"Rob","last_name":"Robins","role":"Ichthyology Collection Manager","email":"rhrobins@flmnh.ufl.edu"},{"first_name":"Rob","last_name":"Robins","role":"Ichthyology Collection Manager","email":"rhrobins@flmnh.ufl.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC4 BY-NC","publisher":"350857a8-4940-4d02-ad42-49557f8006f1","totalCount":240895,"hitRatio":0.000008302372402914132},{"uuid":"8960fcec-05c0-43c5-a83e-87ace7d3091d","itemCount":1,"name":"FHSM Fish Collection","description":"The Ichthyology Collection consists of over 26,000 cataloged lots of fishes, primarily from the Great Plains. Because of recent contracts with both state and federal wildlife agencies, this collection is rapidly growing and has become a major regional depository for Great Plains fishes. At this time, no tissue samples are available.","url":"http://sternberg.fhsu.edu/research-collections/collections/ichthyology/","emllink":"https://ipt.vertnet.org/eml.do?r=fhsm_fish","archivelink":"https://ipt.vertnet.org/archive.do?r=fhsm_fish","contacts":[{"first_name":"Curtis","last_name":"Schmidt","role":"Collections Manager","email":"cjschmidt@fhsu.edu"},{"first_name":"Curtis","last_name":"Schmidt","role":"Collections Manager","email":"cjschmidt@fhsu.edu"},{"first_name":"William","last_name":"Stark","role":"Associate Curator","email":"wstark@fhsu.edu"},{"first_name":"Laura","last_name":"Russell","role":"Programmer","email":"larussell@vertnet.org"},{"first_name":"David","last_name":"Bloom","role":"Coordinator","email":"dbloom@vertnet.org"},{"first_name":"John","last_name":"Wieczorek","role":"Information Architect","email":"tuco@berkeley.edu"},{"first_name":"Curtis","last_name":"Schmidt","role":"Collections Manager","email":"cjschmidt@fhsu.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC0","publisher":"842a2bb5-d705-4d6c-8401-abf3ca28c05d","totalCount":25535,"hitRatio":0.00003916193459956922}],"aggs":{"rs":{"doc_count_error_upper_bound":0,"sum_other_doc_count":0,"buckets":[{"key":"cab6d230-499b-4a21-9cc2-2750e14e92f8","doc_count":7},{"key":"ce0c9488-97f0-432a-a0fa-d204230366be","doc_count":3},{"key":"c38b867b-05f3-4733-802e-d8d2d3324f84","doc_cou